1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,120
If type 2 diabetes means cells respond poorly

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,320
to insulin, why isn't the treatment simply more

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,520
insulin?

4
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:10,000
Early on, many people with type 2 make

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:13,440
plenty of insulin, sometimes more than usual.

6
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,280
Adding more of a signal the cells are

7
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:18,400
already ignoring isn't the first move.

8
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,360
So how can type 2 diabetes be managed?

9
00:00:22,567 --> 00:00:25,526
Earlier, you saw how type 2 develops.

10
00:00:25,767 --> 00:00:29,126
In muscle and fat cells, insulin still binds,

11
00:00:29,207 --> 00:00:32,326
but fewer glucose transporters reach the membrane, so

12
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:34,006
glucose stays in the blood.

13
00:00:34,647 --> 00:00:37,606
The liver also releases too much glucose.

14
00:00:37,927 --> 00:00:40,886
Beta cells cover by releasing more insulin, until

15
00:00:40,967 --> 00:00:41,926
they fall behind.

16
00:00:42,887 --> 00:00:46,126
Type 1 is different: immune cells destroy the

17
00:00:46,167 --> 00:00:48,886
beta cells, so little or no insulin is

18
00:00:48,967 --> 00:00:49,686
made.

19
00:00:50,087 --> 00:00:51,846
Think of insulin as a key.

20
00:00:52,087 --> 00:00:54,246
Type 1 has no key.

21
00:00:54,327 --> 00:00:56,726
In type 2, the key fits, but the

22
00:00:56,807 --> 00:00:58,006
lock is jammed.

23
00:00:59,234 --> 00:01:01,353
So management has two jobs.

24
00:01:01,634 --> 00:01:04,673
Bring blood glucose back towards its usual range,

25
00:01:04,754 --> 00:01:06,513
and lower the risk of damage to blood

26
00:01:06,594 --> 00:01:09,313
vessels, kidneys, eyes and nerves.

27
00:01:10,034 --> 00:01:12,473
Management is the long-term work of keeping a

28
00:01:12,514 --> 00:01:15,313
disease under control, without curing it.

29
00:01:15,874 --> 00:01:18,513
A treatment acts on the disease mechanism.

30
00:01:18,834 --> 00:01:21,913
And monitoring measures whether the plan is working.

31
00:01:22,194 --> 00:01:24,673
A good plan links every action back to

32
00:01:24,754 --> 00:01:25,633
the mechanism.

33
00:01:26,834 --> 00:01:29,313
Start with lifestyle, because it acts on the

34
00:01:29,394 --> 00:01:30,233
cause.

35
00:01:30,514 --> 00:01:33,713
When muscles contract during activity, they move glucose

36
00:01:33,794 --> 00:01:37,393
transporters into the membrane without needing insulin, so

37
00:01:37,474 --> 00:01:38,913
glucose leaves the blood.

38
00:01:39,554 --> 00:01:42,033
Losing weight shrinks the fat stored in and

39
00:01:42,114 --> 00:01:44,753
around the liver and other organs, so cells

40
00:01:44,954 --> 00:01:46,593
respond to insulin better again.

41
00:01:47,234 --> 00:01:49,713
The catch is keeping it up for years,

42
00:01:49,794 --> 00:01:52,513
which depends on time, money and access to

43
00:01:52,674 --> 00:01:53,473
healthy food.

44
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,740
Most people also take a tablet called metformin.

45
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,620
It reduces the glucose the liver releases into

46
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,900
the blood, and helps muscle respond to insulin,

47
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:07,020
so glucose falls without pushing tired beta cells

48
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,220
to work harder.

49
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:11,900
It's cheap, well tested, rarely makes glucose drop

50
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:13,900
too low, and doesn't add weight.

51
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:16,860
But it doesn't remove the resistance, and some

52
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:18,620
people get stomach upsets.

53
00:02:19,834 --> 00:02:21,713
How do you know the plan's working?

54
00:02:21,994 --> 00:02:24,873
One glucose reading only shows that moment.

55
00:02:25,354 --> 00:02:27,993
Glucose slowly sticks to haemoglobin in red blood

56
00:02:28,074 --> 00:02:31,513
cells, and red cells last about four months.

57
00:02:31,634 --> 00:02:34,953
So the HbA1c test, the share of haemoglobin

58
00:02:35,034 --> 00:02:38,233
with glucose attached, shows average glucose over the

59
00:02:38,394 --> 00:02:40,033
past two to three months.

60
00:02:40,314 --> 00:02:42,313
One good morning can't fake it.

61
00:02:42,554 --> 00:02:44,873
Monitoring doesn't lower glucose.

62
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:47,833
It's the evidence for keeping, changing or stepping

63
00:02:47,914 --> 00:02:48,793
up the plan.

64
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,920
If HbA1c stays above target, the plan steps

65
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,280
up: another medicine, and if beta cells keep

66
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,400
falling behind, insulin.

67
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:00,920
Here's the twist.

68
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:04,800
Injected insulin replaces a signal that's running short,

69
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:07,680
but it doesn't unjam the lock, and it

70
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:10,400
can add weight, which worsens the resistance.

71
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:14,560
Care also targets the damage itself: medicines for

72
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:18,000
blood pressure and cholesterol, and regular kidney, eye

73
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,040
and foot checks.

74
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:22,000
They don't treat the diabetes, but they prevent

75
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,120
much of its harm.

76
00:03:24,334 --> 00:03:26,013
How strong is the evidence?

77
00:03:26,494 --> 00:03:29,613
Take DiRECT, a trial in Scotland and England.

78
00:03:30,094 --> 00:03:32,493
GP practices were randomly assigned.

79
00:03:32,894 --> 00:03:35,453
In one group, adults diagnosed in the past

80
00:03:35,534 --> 00:03:38,013
six years had a low-energy diet for several

81
00:03:38,094 --> 00:03:40,733
months, then support to keep the weight off.

82
00:03:41,294 --> 00:03:43,533
Other practices gave usual care.

83
00:03:43,854 --> 00:03:46,253
After a year, 46 per cent of the

84
00:03:46,334 --> 00:03:49,173
diet group were in remission, glucose below the

85
00:03:49,214 --> 00:03:53,693
diabetes threshold without glucose-lowering medicines, against 4 per

86
00:03:53,814 --> 00:03:55,213
cent with usual care.

87
00:03:56,434 --> 00:03:57,393
Now judge it.

88
00:03:57,794 --> 00:04:00,593
It was randomised and the gap was large,

89
00:04:00,674 --> 00:04:02,913
so it's strong evidence that weight loss early

90
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:05,033
on can reverse the disease.

91
00:04:05,314 --> 00:04:07,833
But remission faded as weight came back.

92
00:04:08,114 --> 00:04:11,953
Among 85 people followed with continued support, 11

93
00:04:12,034 --> 00:04:13,633
were in remission at five years.

94
00:04:14,274 --> 00:04:17,713
Participants were recently diagnosed and not on insulin,

95
00:04:17,834 --> 00:04:19,953
so it may not apply more widely.

96
00:04:20,194 --> 00:04:22,113
Everyday results are often smaller.

97
00:04:23,334 --> 00:04:26,213
The syllabus also asks about future research.

98
00:04:26,774 --> 00:04:29,173
One active direction is drugs that copy a

99
00:04:29,254 --> 00:04:31,573
gut hormone called GLP-1.

100
00:04:32,134 --> 00:04:34,853
They make beta cells release insulin only when

101
00:04:34,934 --> 00:04:38,213
glucose is high, slow the stomach emptying, and

102
00:04:38,414 --> 00:04:41,093
reduce appetite, so people eat less and lose

103
00:04:41,174 --> 00:04:41,573
weight.

104
00:04:42,214 --> 00:04:46,053
Large trials show lower HbA1c and weight loss,

105
00:04:46,134 --> 00:04:48,293
and for some drugs, fewer heart attacks and

106
00:04:48,374 --> 00:04:50,213
strokes in people at high risk.

107
00:04:50,854 --> 00:04:54,373
Against that, many are injected, often costly, can

108
00:04:54,454 --> 00:04:57,333
cause nausea, and weight tends to return when

109
00:04:57,414 --> 00:04:58,293
people stop.

110
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:01,140
Two exam questions.

111
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:01,900
First.

112
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:05,020
A person with type 2 diabetes has used

113
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:08,060
metformin and an activity plan for two years.

114
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:12,380
Their HbA1c has risen from 7.0 to 8.4

115
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:16,420
per cent, and their doctor suggests adding insulin.

116
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:20,540
Explain what the HbA1c result shows, and assess

117
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:24,140
whether insulin alone would fix the underlying problem.

118
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:25,740
Pause here to answer.

119
00:05:36,167 --> 00:05:39,686
HbA1c shows average glucose over two to three

120
00:05:39,847 --> 00:05:42,966
months, so a rise from 7.0 to 8.4

121
00:05:43,127 --> 00:05:47,046
means control has worsened over months, not on

122
00:05:47,127 --> 00:05:48,566
one bad day.

123
00:05:48,647 --> 00:05:51,206
The beta cells may be falling further behind,

124
00:05:51,287 --> 00:05:53,526
so stepping up makes sense.

125
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:56,726
But insulin replaces the signal, it doesn't fix

126
00:05:56,767 --> 00:05:59,526
the resistance, and it can add weight.

127
00:05:59,687 --> 00:06:02,806
So keep the activity and metformin too.

128
00:06:02,887 --> 00:06:06,486
The classic mistake is calling HbA1c a treatment.

129
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:08,260
Second.

130
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:11,620
In a trial, 600 adults with type 2

131
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:15,060
diabetes were randomly given a new weekly injection

132
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:18,100
or a placebo for 26 weeks.

133
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:21,700
HbA1c fell by 1.4 points with the drug

134
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:24,620
and 0.3 with the placebo.

135
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:26,740
One in eight stopped the drug because of

136
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:29,820
nausea, and it isn't subsidised yet.

137
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:32,420
Evaluate this evidence for using the drug to

138
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,180
manage type 2 diabetes.

139
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:36,020
Pause here to answer.

140
00:06:46,434 --> 00:06:49,313
It was randomised, with a placebo, so the

141
00:06:49,354 --> 00:06:52,193
bigger fall is most likely the drug's effect,

142
00:06:52,314 --> 00:06:55,313
and 1.1 points is a large change.

143
00:06:55,874 --> 00:06:59,153
But 26 weeks is short, and HbA1c is

144
00:06:59,234 --> 00:07:02,273
a measure, not the outcome people care about:

145
00:07:02,354 --> 00:07:03,953
fewer heart attacks or deaths.

146
00:07:04,594 --> 00:07:07,073
Side effects and cost may stop people using

147
00:07:07,154 --> 00:07:07,313
it.

148
00:07:07,794 --> 00:07:10,273
So it's promising, but not yet proven for

149
00:07:10,354 --> 00:07:11,233
long-term care.

150
00:07:11,874 --> 00:07:14,353
The classic mistake is treating a trial result

151
00:07:14,514 --> 00:07:16,193
as real-world success.

152
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,760
So, for any management question.

153
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,920
Name the mechanism, say how each action changes

154
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,520
it, then judge the evidence: was it randomised,

155
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:28,680
how long did it run, what outcome did

156
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:31,360
it measure, and can people keep it up?

157
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,480
Next, how prevention campaigns can stop disease before

158
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,520
it starts.

159
00:07:37,734 --> 00:07:39,173
Here are the key notes.

160
00:07:39,414 --> 00:07:41,333
Pause the video if you need more time

161
00:07:41,414 --> 00:07:42,213
to copy them.
